The Following is a list of ToolTypes for this ICON:


NOTICE: ALL TOOLTYPES ARE CASE SENSITIVE

ABOUT: This ICON may be any name you wish it to be. You should find some
       pre-defined MODEM.DEFS in the STORAGE/MODEM directory.

       This defines the commands your particular modem requires to perform
       various functions.

       This ICON must be in the NODE/MODEM directory for any node which is
       tied to a modem.


MODEM.INIT=
MODEM.RESET=
MODEM.RING=
MODEM.ANSWER=
MODEM.OFFHOOK=


MODEM.INIT=<string>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express how to initialize your modem.

     MODEM.INIT=ATE0X7&A3


MODEM.RESET=<string>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express how to reset the modem for receiving another call.

     MODEM.RESET=ATH0


MODEM.RING=<string>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express how to notice an incoming call from the modem.

     MODEM.RING=RING


MODEM.ANSWER=<string>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express how to respond to an incoming call from a modem.

     MODEM.ANSWER=ATA


MODEM.OFFHOOK=<string>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express how to take you modem off hook.

     MODEM.OFFHOOK=ATM0H1

